<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
  <Document>
    <name>🌊 LIVE WAVE DIRECTION</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<h2>LIVE WAVE PERIOD & DIRECTION</h2><p><b>Gradient key</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/wave_direction/legend.png" width="600" alt="gradient key"><br>Peak wave period (seconds between crests, as filed by GLWU PERPW): <b>LOWEST 0s</b> dark-blue flat &rarr; <b>2</b> blue &rarr; <b>3</b> cyan &rarr; <b>4</b> green &rarr; <b>5</b> yellow &rarr; <b>6</b> orange &rarr; <b>7.5</b> red &rarr; <b>9</b> magenta &rarr; <b>10.5</b> violet &rarr; <b>HIGHEST+ 12s</b> dark-purple long swell. Same seconds always show the same color; values above 12s stay dark-purple. Arrows point where the waves are traveling (WVDIR filed direction + 180&deg;). Lake max now: <b>7.0s</b>, mean <b>2.7s</b>, mean travel <b>33&deg; (NE)</b>.</p><p>This entry auto-refreshes from the live overlay (source: NOAA/NCEP Great Lakes Wave Unstructured v2.1 (GLWUv2.1, WAVEWATCH III) — PERPW peak period + WVDIR direction, surface analysis).<br/><b>Data time:</b> 2026-09-25 09:00 PM EDT<br/><b>Source version:</b> glwu-20260926-0100Z-wvperiod<br/><b>Status:</b> LIVE / CURRENT MODEL (analysis), 6-hourly cycles</p><p>Turn on/off independently of all other layers. Add this file once; new source cycles appear automatically.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
    <NetworkLink>
      <name>🌊 LIVE WAVE DIRECTION — auto-refresh</name>
      <Link>
